  :adr/body "# ADR 2799007516: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7516 Tobacco Preparers and Tobacco Products Makers factory-floor scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7516\n-- Tobacco Preparers and Tobacco Products Makers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-7 already landed, ~42 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7516\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7516\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Tobacco Preparers and Tobacco Products Makers\"\n-- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7516` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7516` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nTobacco preparers and tobacco products makers manufacture a heavily\nregulated product -- alongside standard workshop safety hazards\n(equipment exposure, dust exposure), this vertical carries a\nregulatory-compliance dimension specific to the manufacturing process\nitself (tax-stamp affixing and labeling-compliance determinations),\ndistinct from downstream age-verification-of-sale concerns which are\nout of scope for a manufacturer. The controlling constraint for this\nvertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a regulatory-compliance-clearance decision\n(tax-stamp affixing sign-off, labeling-compliance determination) or a\nmanufacturing-execution decision, nor override a shop safety officer's\njudgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent block or\nan always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to FACTORY-FLOOR SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never performs manufacturing work or makes\nregulatory-compliance-clearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\nclosely-related regulated-manufacturing-clearance safety pattern) --\ncloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7516` as an OSS factory-floor\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for tobacco preparers and\ntobacco products makers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Tobacco Preparation Coordination Advisor ⊣\nTobaccoCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **factory-floor scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct manufacturing-execution or\nregulatory-compliance-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nmanufacturing-execution decision, a regulatory-compliance-clearance\ndecision (tax-stamp affixing, labeling-compliance determination), or\nany override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from\nthe op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/machine-schedule scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-compliance-concern` -- surface a regulatory-compliance/\n  equipment-hazard/dust-exposure concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- tobacco-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nmanufacturing-execution decision or a regulatory-compliance-clearance\ndecision (tax-stamp affixing, labeling-compliance determination) or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation\n-- an op such as `:affix-tax-stamp` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names nine\nconcretely-forbidden ops\n(`tobaccocoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-manufacturing-decision`, `:authorize-production-run`,\n`:proceed-with-production-run`, `:finalize-production-decision`,\n`:affix-tax-stamp`, `:finalize-tax-stamp-compliance-decision`,\n`:finalize-labeling-compliance-determination`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`tobaccocoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-manufacturing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-production-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-affix-tax-stamp`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-labeling-compliance-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Preparer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered preparer record (`:no-preparer`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the preparer is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered manufacturing facility (`:no-facility`).\n   Together with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL\n   invariant that a worker/facility record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the nine\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   production run, affixing a tax stamp, finalizing a\n   labeling-compliance determination, or overriding a shop safety\n   officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks manufacturing-execution/regulatory-compliance-\n   clearance/safety-override language wherever it appears in free\n   text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-compliance-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless\n  of confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a regulatory-compliance/\n  equipment-hazard/dust-exposure observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the compliance\n  or hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  compliance clearance or shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  tobacco-materials order is not itself unsafe or non-compliant,\n  unlike a manufacturing-execution/regulatory-compliance-clearance or\n  safety-officer-override attempt, which is why it is handled by a\n  different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"tobacco\", \"tax stamp\", \"labeling\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a factory-floor coordination actor\nworking adjacent to tobacco preparation and tax-stamp/labeling\ncompliance necessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/\nlogging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`tobaccocoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the production\nrun\", \"affix the tax stamp\", \"finalize the labeling compliance\ndetermination\", \"override the shop safety officer's judgment\" --\nmatching the task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns,\nand\n`tobaccocoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for preparer ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\ntobacco-preparation task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`tobaccocoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-manufacturing-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand\n`tobaccocoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-tax-stamp-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7516\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7516` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7516`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 24 tests, 52 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-tax-stamp-application` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  regulatory-compliance-clearance decision exists in the code path and\n  is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (tax\n  law and product-labeling compliance, plus physical equipment/dust-\n  exposure hazards), the capability itself must not exist. The only\n  op related to compliance escalation is `:flag-compliance-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer/compliance-\n  function attention and never itself decides, clears, or defers a\n  regulatory-compliance-clearance decision for later automatic\n  execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold tobacco-materials\n  order is not itself unsafe or non-compliant, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  manufacturing-execution/regulatory-compliance-clearance/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"tobacco\" \"tax stamp\"\n  \"labeling\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses tobacco/\n  tax-stamp/labeling/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/\n  logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against\n  rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Collapsing the regulatory-compliance-clearance dimension\n  (tax-stamp/labeling) and the workshop-safety dimension (equipment/\n  dust hazard) into a single generic \"compliance\" op class without\n  distinguishing the two forbidden-decision categories: rejected --\n  the task explicitly names both a regulatory-compliance-clearance\n  decision (tax-stamp affixing sign-off, labeling-compliance\n  determination) AND a manufacturing-execution decision as distinct\n  hard-blocked categories, alongside a distinct shop-safety-officer-\n  override block, so this ADR and the governor's op/phrase lists name\n  all three explicitly rather than merging them into one vaguer\n  category.\n- Merging `preparer` and `facility` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered preparer AND\n  independently-registered facility) matches the CRITICAL invariant\n  that a \"worker/facility record must be independently verified/\n  registered before any action\" and the established pattern from\n  prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance\n  checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered preparer AND facility\n   (`:no-preparer`/`:no-facility`). Not a manufacturing-execution or\n   regulatory-compliance-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/machine-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a manufacturing-execution\n   decision (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such\n   attempt via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action`\n   content check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any\n   conclusion about a specific production run -- it is a calendar/\n   logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-compliance-concern`** -- surfaces a regulatory-compliance/\n   equipment-hazard/dust-exposure concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer/compliance function; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at\n   every confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the\n   ONLY channel through which a compliance or safety observation may\n   be surfaced, and it explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on\n   anything itself -- the shop safety officer or compliance function\n   reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- tobacco-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a manufacturing-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na manufacturing-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nproduction run), a regulatory-compliance-clearance decision (e.g.\naffixing a tax stamp or finalizing a labeling-compliance\ndetermination), or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these\ncategories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the\nclosed four-op allowlist itself (`tobaccocoord.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) nine concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`tobaccocoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`tobaccocoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-manufacturing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-production-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-affix-tax-stamp`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-labeling-compliance-determination`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`tobaccocoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a production run, affix a tax stamp, or\noverride a shop safety officer's judgment even via an\notherwise-allowlisted op\n(`tobaccocoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-production-run-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-tax-stamp-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"
